  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 113 AM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nA broad upper level trough with embedded shortwaves will become a \nbit more amplified though this evening, providing modest \nforcing for a 20-50% chance of intermittent showers and \nthunderstorms. The greatest risk peaks this evening, especially\nacross portions of southern Illinois and southeast Missouri \nwhen storms capable of causing heavy downpours and lightning \nwill be possible. Despite weak shear, cannot rule out a stray \nstrong gusty storm given DCAPE over 1000 J/kg combined with \n7.5-8.0 C/km 0-3km lapse rates and a 30-40K theta-e difference. \nLow rain chances shift east of the Mississippi and linger \nthrough most of Saturday before diminishing. Total rainfall \nbetween a tenth of an inch to a half inch remains progged with \nlocally higher amounts.\n\nAs an upper level ridge builds more east over the weekend, the heat \nand humidity will be on the increase. Daily high temperatures \nranging from the upper 80s to lower 90s with dewpoints in the \nlow to mid 70s will potentially yield 4 consecutive days of heat\nindex values rising above 100 to around 105 degrees, and may \neventually require a Heat Advisory in the future. A few \nlocations may even reach 100 today, but the potential for \nconvection and cloud debris will likely keep this too limited to\nwarrant any headlines for the duration criteria. While a brief \nlull in the unsettled weather will occur Sunday into Monday with\ntranquil conditions, the ridge quickly breaks down towards the \nmiddle of the week with daily chances of showers and \nthunderstorms making a return beginning late Tuesday into \nWednesday. Temperatures eventually trend near to slightly below \nnormal in the latter half of the week as a cold front sweeps \nthrough.",
